# Line endings are normalised to LF in the repository AND on checkout.
#
# Not cosmetic. Before this file, CRLF was committed into the blobs themselves,
# so a Linux CI runner checked out CRLF and prettier reported one error per
# line — over twenty thousand of them — which would have made the lint gate
# unusable on its first run. `eol=lf` (not just `text=auto`) also stops Windows
# checkouts from reintroducing CR, so the class cannot come back.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be touched by the eol filter.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
